message.content:
Now I need to understand the UAF. Let me look at `msFreeProjection` and `msFreeMap` to understand what gets freed. The key insight is in `loadProjection`:

```c
if( i == 1 && strstr(p->args[0],"+") != NULL ) {
  char *one_line_def = p->args[0];
  p->args[0] = NULL;
  result = msLoadProjectionString( p, one_line_def );
  free( one_line_def );
  return result;
}
```

`msLoadProjectionString` calls `msFreeProjectionExceptContext(p)` which calls `msFreeProjection(p)`. Let me look at `msFreeProjection`:

content:
631:void msFreeProjection(projectionObj *p)
658:void msFreeProjectionExceptContext(projectionObj *p)
void msFreeProjection(projectionObj *p)
{
#if PROJ_VERSION_MAJOR >= 6
  proj_destroy(p->proj);
  p->proj = NULL;
  msProjectionContextUnref(p->proj_ctx);
  p->proj_ctx = NULL;
#else
  if(p->proj) {
    pj_free(p->proj);
    p->proj = NULL;
  }
#if PJ_VERSION >= 480
  if(p->proj_ctx) {
    pj_ctx_free(p->proj_ctx);
    p->proj_ctx = NULL;
  }
#endif
#endif

  p->gt.need_geotransform = MS_FALSE;
  p->wellknownprojection = wkp_none;
  msFreeCharArray(p->args, p->numargs);
  p->args = NULL;
  p->numargs = 0;
}
